Your resume must demonstrate at least one year of specialized experience at or equivalent to the GS-11 grade level or pay band in the Federal service or equivalent experience in the private or public sector. Specialized experience must demonstrate the following: (1) Planning, directing, and coordinating work of a branch and promoting efficient and economical work operations;
(2) Solving problems by identifying and analyzing problems, evaluating solutions, and making recommendations;
(3) Providing customer service to internal and external customers by delivering products and services, and committing to continuous process improvement;
(4) Conducting supply management duties by use of Maximo, supply management principles, inventory accountability, and warehouse or shop stores processes;
(5) Applying management and leadership principles, and personnel regulations and policies to manage the personnel and workload;
(6) Completing physical management reporting, financial reports, and data calls and
(7) Communicating effectively both orally and in writing, ability to read and interpret instructions, supply documents, Maximo reports and material job plans. Additional qualification information can be found from the following Office of Personnel Management web site: https://www.opm.gov/policy-data-oversight/classification-qualifications/general-schedule-qualification-standards/#url=List-by-Occupational-Series Experience refers to paid and unpaid experience, including volunteer work done through National Service programs (e.g., professional, philanthropic, religious, spiritual, community, student, social). Volunteer work helps build critical competencies, knowledge, and skills and can provide valuable training and experience that translates directly to paid employment.

