Your resume must demonstrate at least one year of specialized experience performing work concerned with receiving, handling, storing, maintaining while in storage, issuing, or physically controlling items within a storage and distribution system equivalent to the next lower grade level (GS-07) or pay band in the federal service or equivalent experience in the private or public sector. Specialized experience must demonstrate performing duties such as:
1) Performing storage projections to ensure adequate storage area is available for inbound material and staged material awaiting disposal;
2) Identifying problem areas, to recommend corrective action, to provide technical data, and to develop reports to provide metrics for management review;
3) Coordinating with disposition services to schedule appointments for the turn-in of disposal material and pick-up of remain-in-place material. FOR GS-07 Your resume must demonstrate at least one year of specialized experience performing work concerned with receiving, handling, storing, maintaining while in storage, issuing, or physically controlling items within a storage and distribution system equivalent to the next lower grade level (GS-05) or pay band in the federal service or equivalent experience in the private or public sector. Specialized experience must demonstrate performing duties such as:
1) Identifying and validating material and material for disposal, and obtaining disposition instructions;
2) Ensuring the accuracy of data fields such as stock number, unit of issue demilitarization code, classification code, project code and condition code to create expenditure documents for disposal material;
3) Operating a variety of Material Handling Equipment (MHE) to assist with pulling of material and to verify inventory discrepancies. Additional qualification information can be found from the following Office of Personnel Management web site: https://www.opm.gov/policy-data-oversight/classification-qualifications/general-schedule-qualification-standards/#url=List-by-Occupational-Series Experience refers to paid and unpaid experience, including volunteer work done through National Service programs (e.g., professional, philanthropic, religious, spiritual, community, student, social). Volunteer work helps build critical competencies, knowledge, and skills and can provide valuable training and experience that translates directly to paid employment.

